{
  "provenance": "AUTHORED 2026-08-17, Wave 2 Track D. This table is the whole mapping from GameEvent to spell VFX; src/render/vfx/**.ts contains no spell id and no `if (spellId === ...)`, and VfxSystem.test.ts greps for both. A new spell is a new row here.",
  "vocabulary": "Every `match.spellId` below must name an APPROVED spell in public/content/magic.json. loadCueTable() takes the spell vocabulary as an option and reports an `unknown-spell` defect for a row that names one that is not authored, the same way GateEngine refuses a rule naming an unauthored receiver. A test loads this file against the shipped records and asserts zero defects, so a renamed or cut spell fails the build rather than leaving a cue that can never fire.",
  "colour": "`colorKey` is a key of COLOR in src/ui/theme.ts, which is contrast-checked. A raw hex here is an `unknown-color-key` defect, and a companion test greps every .ts file in this folder for a hex literal so the renderer cannot introduce one either.",
  "ordering": "FIRST MATCH WINS, so the per-spell rows sit above the generic ones. findUnreachableRules() computes the rows an earlier row already covers and a test asserts the list is empty.",
  "noEffectHonesty": "Every approved spell has BOTH a `cast:resolved`/effect row and a `cast:resolved`/no-effect row — that much is still enforced (VfxSystem.test.ts: 'plays something — never nothing at all'). No red, no shake: VfxTone has no failure member, the loader refuses `danger` on any landed cast, and it refuses an error-ish token in a row's id or params, on EITHER row, unconditionally.",
  "noEffectWeightPolicy": "RELAXED 2026-08-22 (Roc, the VFX prototype batch). The original rule required a no-effect row to be identical to its effect twin in kind/tone/duration/every shape param, differing only by colour (and for `tint`, `amount`), so the two landed within 5% of the same on-screen weight. That is still good practice and `breath`/`fetch`/`weigh` still follow it — but it is no longer mandatory. A spell's VFX firing at all is the signal a cast happened; it does not have to be the same shape dimmed down, and an effect row is free to be more elaborate than its no-effect twin. `cueWeight`/`neutralFor` in CueTable.ts remain correct and available for any pair still authored that way.",
  "neutralRuleWhenUsed": "Where a pair IS weight-matched (see above), the no-effect colour is DERIVED, not chosen: of the theme's neutral keys (`ink`, `muted` — the only two that carry no meaning), take the one whose cueWeight() lands closest to the effect twin's, and never one that reads more than 5% dimmer. `neutralFor()` in CueTable.ts is that rule as code.",
  "tintAmounts": "`weigh`'s old `tint` pair (superseded by `suspend`) compensated `amount`, because a tint's visible depth is `amount * (1 - min channel)` and `muted` bites harder than the effect colours do: 0.25 -> 0.2061, solved so the rendered weights matched within 0.1%. Kept here as a worked example — `amount` is the one param pure strength with no geometry in it, which is why it is the only one a weight-matched `tint` pair may differ in.",
  "reach": "Only rows whose event type is EMITTED and whose emitter sits in a scene that mounts a VfxSystem can ever play. `cue.craft.completed`, `cue.item.acquired.forage` and `cue.item.acquired.any` were removed because nothing in src/ emits `craft:completed` or `item:acquired` at all — three rows that looked authored and could never fire. The gate and receiver rows are kept and DECLARED: GateEngine and ReceiverStateStore do emit them, but no scene constructs either yet (Wave 2 Track B), so VfxSystem.test.ts lists them in AWAITING_WIRING and fails both if a new dead row appears and if a declared one becomes reachable and is not removed from the list.",
  "default": {
    "id": "cue.default.neutral",
    "kind": "none",
    "tone": "quiet",
    "durationMs": 0
  },
